{:id :EACL-FORMAL-014
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :manual-review
 :seed-or-trace
 "subproblem-cache/parent-future/child-future/inherited-same-key"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :availability
 :affected-versions
 ["PR 101 worktree before context-aware recursive-self execution"]
 :affected-backends [:shared :datomic :datascript :datahike]
 :root-cause
 "A recursive same-key `resolve!` bypassed its shared flight by invoking `compute` directly. Clojure futures inherit dynamic bindings, so a child thread could inherit the parent's resolving-key set, take the self-bypass, and run a callback that was absent from the coordinator's active-callback count."
 :fix
 "The final v8 cache deletes computation slots, permits, shared flights, and recursive self-bypass. Every miss performs its own request-bounded computation and publication is a bounded nonblocking optimization."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.datomic.trusted-surface-audit-test/deleted-trusted-surfaces-stay-deleted-test"
  "eacl.formal.cache-strategy-adversarial-test/publication-and-independent-computation-traces-exhaustive-test"]}
